A:

The simplest way to provide this would be to just brute force the query through a list of available products. 
If you don't want me to do that, then you'll have to figure out how to use Elasticsearch and Elasticsearch's indexing facilities
To setup a product index in Index Name=products in your Elasticsearch instance, try:
index products --actions 'flatten'

You'll want to set up the following settings, as well:
--actions 'keyword' index.properties ['tags']
--actions 'keyword' index.properties '[sources]'

You might also find the following snippet helpful, just making sure that you're searching appropriately for "String Trimmer" as a single word:
{
      "query": {
          "match_all": {
              "query": {
                  "match_phrase": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "query": "string trimmer:string"
                  }
              }
          }
      }
}

There are a few questions and answers (see this post) that would address some other ways to improve upon this solution, too.
